  "lyrics": {
    "song_name": "Fast Car",
    "artist_name": "Tracy Chapman",
    "lyrics_text": "you get a fast car \n    i wanted to get to anywhere \nmaybe we make a deal \nmaybe together we can get somewhere \nany is better \nstarting from zero \ngot nothing to lose \nmaybe we'll make something \nme myself i got nothing to prove\n\nyou got a fatter scarf \ni a plan to get us out of here \nbeen working at the convenience store \nmanaged to save just a little bit of money \nwon't have to drive too far \njust across the border and into the city \nyou and i can book your job \nand find and see what it means to be a living\n\nsee my old man's got a problem \nyeah but the bottle that's the way it is \nhe says body's too old for working \nbody's too young to look alike yes \nbut mama went off and left him \nshe wanted more of a life than he could give \ni said somebody's got to take care of him \ni quit school and that's what i did\n\nyou gotta fast car \nis it fast enough so we could fly away \nyou gotta make a decision \ntonight and live and die this way\n\nso remember when you were driving in your car \nspeed of bicycle like i was drunk \nso didn't i stay up before \ncan your arms run like crap around my shoulder \ni had a feeling that i belong \ni had a feeling i could see someone see someone see someone\n\ngot a fast car \nwe go cruise and entertain ourselves \nstill ain't got a job \nnow work in the market as a checkout girl \ni know things will get better \nyou'll find working out get promoted \nand we'll move out of the shelter \nbuy a bigger house and live in the suburbs\n\nso i remember when we were driving \ndriving in your car \nspeed are back it's i got was drunk \nit didn't i stay out before yeah i'm feeling nice about my children \ni i had a feeling that i belong \ni i a feeling i could be someone be someone be someone\n\nyou a fast car \ni got a job that pays all our bills \nit's now freaking big at the bottom \nmore your friends than you do your kids \ni'd always hope for better \nbut maybe together you and me find it \nthey got no plans i ain't going nowhere \ntake your best car and keep on driving\n\nso i remember when we were driving \ndriving in your car \nsees the back like i was drunk \ndidn't i stay out you're on the next around my shoulder \ni i had a feeling that i belong \ni i had a feeling i could be someone be someone be someone\n\nyou gotta fast god \nis it fast enough so you can fly away \nyou gotta make a decision \nleave tonight or live and die this way",
